    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math interesting but not deeply connected to my daily life. My vocational diploma included basic math, and I used it in practical tasks like budgeting or measuring. I appreciate its logic and structure, especially in art and design where symmetry and patterns matter. I don’t see it as a core part of who I am, but I respect its role in understanding the world.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve never felt overwhelmed by math in a way that causes anxiety. When I encounter a complex problem, I take a deep breath and break it into small parts—like how I do with board games or knitting. My Buddhist background helps me stay calm, focusing on the process rather than outcomes. Math is just another puzzle to solve, not a threat.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used a simple AI app to learn basic algebra for a personal project. It gave me step-by-step explanations and visual graphs. I found it helpful, especially for understanding how equations work. It didn’t replace my thinking, but it made me feel more confident. I appreciate how it breaks down problems gently, like a patient friend.",
