    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explaining concepts in simple, relatable ways—like how I explain knitting patterns or board games. They can adapt to different learning styles and provide instant feedback. In classrooms, they could support teachers by generating practice problems or visual aids. This makes math more accessible, especially for students who feel left behind or anxious."
